  "description": {
    "format": "nuke_help_html",
    "plain_text": "This is a Precomp node. The contents of this node come from an external Nuke script. Think of this like a Group that references its content from an external file rather than storing it in this file. You might use a Precomp to manage complexity by breaking parts of your project out into separate comps that can be versioned and edited independently or to share work by allowing multiple artists to work on separate components that contribute to a larger comp.",
    "source": "nuke.Node.help()",
    "text": "<p>This is a Precomp node.  The contents of this node come from an external Nuke script. Think of this like a Group that references its content from an external file rather than storing it in this file.</p><p>You might use a Precomp to manage complexity by breaking parts of your project out into separate comps that can be versioned and edited independently or to share work by allowing multiple artists to work on separate components that contribute to a larger comp.</p>"
  },
